def build_adjacency_list(n, edges, directed=False):
    graph = {i: [] for i in range(n)}
    for u, v, w in edges:
        graph[u].append((v, w))
        if not directed:
            graph[v].append((u, w))   # mirror the edge for undirected graphs
    return graph
```

This is the shape almost every graph algorithm in this group builds on top of — BFS, DFS, Dijkstra, and Prim's all iterate `graph[node]` to get weighted neighbors. Getting this helper right once means every later algorithm reuses it unchanged.
